I have thoroughly explored the repository. Here are my findings.

## Overview
This is a Spring PetClinic REST variant using OfficeFloor. The create-owner flow is a pipeline defined in a YAML file, with each step implemented by a small function class under `.../rest/function/owner/`.

## 1. Registration date set/defaulted
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`
```java
15	    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) {
16	        if (request.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
17	            request.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
18	        }
19	    }
```
If the request supplies a date it is kept; otherwise it defaults to `LocalDate.now()` (plain server date, no adjustment). Wired in the POST pipeline as step `defaultRegistrationDate` (runs after `normalizeEmail`, before `build`).

Field storage on the model: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` lines 55-56 (`@Column(name = "registration_date") private LocalDate registrationDate;`) with getter/setter at 105-111.

OpenAPI contract: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2042-2047 ("Optional; defaults to the server's current date when not supplied").

DB columns (`registration_date DATE`): h2 schema.sql:39, hsqldb:46, mysql:36, postgres:34.

## 2. Membership number generation (year segment from registration date)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMembershipNumber.java`
```java
15	    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
16	        int yy = owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100;
17	        owner.setMembershipNumber(String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy));
18	    }
```
Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where the year segment is the last two digits of `registrationDate.getYear()`. Runs as pipeline step `assignMembershipNumber`, after `assignCustomerCode` and before `assignHouseholdId`/`save`.

Related: `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` builds the `customerCode` (`<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`). Model field `membership_number` at Owner.java:67-68, getter/setter 137-143. OpenAPI description at openapi.yml:2107-2109. DB columns: h2:43, hsqldb:50, mysql:40, postgres:38.

## 3. Daily create-limit (counts owners per day)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUnderDailyLimit.java`
```java
17	    static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;
18	
19	    public void service(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyLimitExceededException {
20	        LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
21	        if (Registrations.countOn(ownerRepository, today) >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
22	            throw new DailyLimitExceededException(today, DAILY_LIMIT);
23	        }
24	    }
```
The per-day count is in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Registrations.java`:
```java
20	    static long countOn(OwnerRepository ownerRepository, LocalDate date) {
21	        return ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
22	                .filter(existing -> date.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
23	                .count();
24	    }
```
Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the given date. Wired as pipeline step `ensureUnderDailyLimit` (after `ensureCityUnderCapacity`, before `normalizeEmail`).

Note: the limit check runs against `LocalDate.now()` (step order: before `defaultRegistrationDate`), and counts owners by their stored `registrationDate`.

Supporting escalation:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyLimitExceededException.java` (holds date + limit, message).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` (responds HTTP 429).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyLimitExceededException.yml` (registers the handler).

## 4. Tests
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (entire file):
```java
9	/** business-day: the default registration date must fall on a business day (a weekend rolls
10	 * forward to Monday). Can't force the server's clock black-box, so assert the invariant that holds
11	 * every day: the default registrationDate is never a Saturday or Sunday. */
12	class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
14		@Test
15		void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
16			int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
17			DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
18			assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
19		}
20	}
```
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` has supporting helpers: `createMany(int n)` (lines 181-187, "all dated today — used to drive the per-day create-limit / bulk-signup rules"), `fillCity` (170-179), `fetchOwner` (199-204), and a comment at line 37 listing the rules (membership number, per-day cap, per-city cap). There are no dedicated membership-number or explicit daily-limit-count test methods beyond these; only the business-day registration-date test exists.

## 5. OfficeFloor REST YAML + function classes for owner creation
POST pipeline: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Full step order:
`normalizeAddress` → `validate` (ValidateOwnerFields) → `normalizeTelephone` → `ensureUniqueTelephone` → `ensureUniqueHousehold` → `ensureCityUnderCapacity` → **`ensureUnderDailyLimit`** → `normalizeEmail` → **`defaultRegistrationDate`** → `build` (BuildOwner) → `assignNamesakeCount` → `assignCustomerCode` → **`assignMembershipNumber`** → `assignHouseholdId` → `save` (SaveOwner) → `respond` (RespondWithOwnerCreated). Endpoint authorizes `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.

All function classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/` (BuildOwner, SaveOwner, AssignOwnerCustomerCode, AssignOwnerNamesakeCount, AssignHouseholdId, RespondWithOwnerCreated, etc.). Other owner endpoints: `owners.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.GET/PUT/DELETE.yml`, `v2/owners.GET.yml`.

## Notable discrepancy (potential bug)
The acceptance test `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` requires the defaulted `registrationDate` to never be Saturday/Sunday (weekend rolls forward to Monday), but `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate` uses a plain `LocalDate.now()` with no business-day rolling. A repo-wide search for any business-day logic (`business.?day|DayOfWeek|SATURDAY|SUNDAY|weekend|rollForward|nextBusiness|isWeekend`) in `src/main` returned nothing — so this rule is asserted by the test but not implemented in production code.

